My eighth valk is running...  (and a monk with AC -43 still alive...)

There are altars on Dlvl 1, 3 and 4.  She converted all of them.  For 
one she needed 4 tries, and became unlucky in between (wand of 
enlightenment), so she explored the mines down to the town.  Bought a 
magic whistle and a stethoscope.  She has a (BoH, too.

On Dlvl 4, there is also a frozen-food store.  First, she did not see 
too much use in it, after having inspected all the ice boxes.  There 
were two floating eye corpses, which might be useful to regain telepathy 
later, several nymph corpses and a leprechaun corpse, not useful right 
now.  There were also several corpses that might give poison resistance, 
but she has it already.  Ate two gray oozes in the hope of getting fire 
resistance, but no luck.

Then it dawned on her that this might be very good luck after all.  The 
pathway from the shop to the temple was quite long, but having a 
pick-axe and being satiated, she was quite happy to get some exercise to 
shorten it.  Then came the crucial test.  Bought a light corpse.  Threw 
it on the altar, sacrificed.  Yes, my god *likes* frozen food.  Well, it 
was clear that this was Mjollnir with almost certainty, given that I had 
more than 300 $ and each single corpse seems to cost 6 $ exactly.

So it was.  First sacrificing gave her lots of four-leaf clovers, then a 
pet unicorn, another one, and finally Mjollnir.  She decided to continue 
sacrificing right away until she could pray, which she used to convert 
her potion of water into holy water.  She sacrificed a little more and 
got Deluder.  Well, since she had already bought a cloak of magic 
resistance in the town one level further down, her "wise use" of this 
gift consisted in stashing it in her bag.  I actually don't understand 
what this "artifact" is good for.  It is a cloak of displacement but 
without AC bonus and with the ordinary magic cancellation for a cloak of 
displacement.  Therefore, nice if you don't have a good cloak at all. 
But worse than a cloak of magic resistance.  Or does it have any useful 
properties I am not aware of?

This valk starts looking good with her AC of -10 and Mojo.  I'll head of 
for Sokoban next and then (if I survive :-) ) for the bottom of the mines.

But it is nice how the game offers you surprises even after having 
played it for a long time.  That a frozen-food store could become *that* 
useful is s.th. I had not been aware of.  If you have it in the right 
place, it provides a much safer way to get an artifact than a wand of 
create monster or create horde (she did not have either anyway, but 
those wands always carry the risk that the monster(s) you create might 
be too tough for you, so to use them safely, you should also have a 
scroll of teleportation ready).
